+# Judiciary independent evidence report — cycle `3e577947f99ad8f4c5bf8349ad20df54`
+
+Issued 2026-11-24 (UTC) by the independent Viche Judiciary under Acts 4 and 15.
+Submitted to Parliament as evidence for consideration. This report does **not** propose, sponsor,
+ratify or implement any reform to measurement systems, audit algorithms, institutional rules
+or the Judiciary's own operation (Act 15 §2). It changes no law, ballot, gate, case state or
+Founder-owned file. Verdicts and dispositions are auditable assertions, not machine proofs.
+
+## Executive summary
+
+The frozen sample of four cases was adjudicated in full by this cycle (all four verdicts already
+filed at 1795544125; not re-filed as a fresh sample). Results: **two `finding`, one
+`not_assigned`, one `inconclusive`**. The findings are an Act 9 host-policy finding (managed-agent
+execution outside `billy-dev`, not CI) on an unassigned scientific issue, and an Act 21/31
+verification-evidence finding on a government-scope decision that is present on `main` but has
+no exact-commit/tree suite record or Act 31 delivery carrier.
+
+One mandatory cross-branch corrective case remained open (`judiciary_mailbox_pending:1795561163`).
+Its pending report — a second, structural integrator stall — was independently investigated and
+dispositioned **"confirmed and still open as to root cause"; the immediate queued-delivery
+blockage self-recovered, not repaired**. The report was preserved and moved to `reviewed/`.
+
+The one-time retrospective correction review was already complete before this session (dated
+addenda of 2026-11-22 on both founder-correction reports). No new substantive evidence supports
+revisiting it; no repeat was performed. All four `continuity_unverified` cases were already
+closed with matching `verified-*.json` receipts; no new continuity filing was warranted.
+
+## 1. Sampled cases (frozen cohort; reproducible selection)
+
+Selection file: `state/oversight/audit-selection-3e577947f99ad8f4c5bf8349ad20df54.json`,
+snapshot SHA256 `9caf2c7cd84e12cfa6814afbd3b13e135d08fbb442636cea76d03190ff156ad3`, seed-after
+stored. Universe 506 items: 375 `claimed_delivery`, 40 `government_decision`, 91 `ignored_work`.
+Four cases drawn (2 open issues, 1 closed claim, 1 government decision).
+
+| Case | Population | Verdict | Substantive result |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `8827779900dfce56a7` / issue `TlqMBqsXlzLrm0TQ1FspnB-snub` | ignored_work | `not_assigned` | Legislature-only Act 32 inquiry; 1 comment by "Viche Executive Innovation Office" headed "inquiry only"; zero authors exactly `Vitalik`; no `billy-dev` execution target. Act 9.2 creates no duty. Clean **not-assigned**, not a verified delivery. |
+| `b2033808150904142b` / issue `Fz2R6jPtA0dzrkMgVuxD0f-solomon` | ignored_work | `finding` | No `billy-dev` assignment and no exact-`Vitalik` comment, so **no neglect finding**. Host-policy finding only: scheduler/agent comments on 2026-11-24 place managed workers on `marceline-dev` while quoting "Execution-Host billy-dev … overrides older". GitHub-hosted CI on ottojung/ivanka PRs is explicitly allowed and was not the basis of the finding. Host inferred from board self-reports, not telemetry. |
+| `9b8bf3ec5cb37b07e5` / issue `205` | claimed_delivery | `inconclusive` | Closed 2026-10-17 with release-captain "locally complete" claim (42 runs/228 assertions, three mutations caught). Earlier history places the fix on local, explicitly unpushed branches. No QAI/Proviral clone on this host and unauthenticated `git ls-remote` fails, so I could not re-run tests or confirm an artifact. Not a false-delivery finding; missing positive evidence counts against the success claim, not as misconduct. |
+| `811f1270eef6f581e2` / decision commit `fc4498e1…` | government_decision | `finding` | PnP bootstrap is an ancestor of `origin/main` (effect real), changing 17 government/tests files. `records/suite-status.json` at that commit and its child names a different candidate (`17f7498e`/tree `fd138ee0`); no `git log -S` record and no `delivery/landed.jsonl` row names `fc4498e1`. Act 21 §5 / Act 31 verification-evidence failure, **not** red tests, not unlawful enactment, not a CI finding. |
+
+The sampled government decision is especially informative: it is the second PnP-bootstrap
+case in this cycle's evidence with the same gate-recording defect, so the defect is not a
+one-off sample artifact.
+
+## 2. Open corrective case and mailbox disposition
+
+Case `judiciary_mailbox_pending:1795561163` (10 observations, 0 clear at last read) is
+**still open**; an absent or self-cleared signal is not a resolution and I did not edit case state.
+
+Pending report: `20261124T2255Z-recovery-steward-integrator-recurrent-suite-hang.md` (an addendum
+to the 21:59Z c1a0000b report). Independent disposition filed at
+`state/oversight/judiciary-mailbox/reviewed/20261124T2255Z-…judiciary-disposition.md`; the original
+report was preserved and moved to `reviewed/`. Evidence established independently:
+
+- Git publication gap on `origin/main`: last carrier `809fdca6` at **22:32:36Z**, next carrier
+  `185d5dbb` at **22:57:41Z** — ~25 minutes. Candidate `3d0714c7` was integrated at 22:32:44Z
+  but received its exact-commit green suite carrier only at 22:57:41Z.
+- `state/delivery/integrator/run.log`: eight `internal lock busy` refusals from 22:32:50Z to
+  23:03:12Z.
+- `government/integrator.py:477–482` on `main` and on the operator's proposed branch head
+  `2e9152ca`: `subprocess.run([...suite-status.sh...])` has **no `timeout=`**, while the run holds
+  the single `internal.lock`. This is the independently verified architectural root cause.
+- The queued record-only deliveries landed 23:03:41–23:05:27Z with their own green Act 21 carriers
+  (`6db4b9fc`, `ead89e19`, `38aad7dc`, `ac3eebaf`, `ea1bd171`). The blockage resolved by queue
+  resumption, not by a repair.
+- The in-progress operator patch adds deadlines to `git()` subprocesses only; it does not bound
+  the suite-status wait and is not landed. No fix is present on `main`.
+
+Disposition: **confirmed and still open as to root cause; immediate blockage resolved by
+self-recovery; not `verified_fixed`.** Owner for repair: operator/Executive machinery owner.
+Judiciary did not kill a process, replay a side effect, change a gate, or implement a timeout.
+
+## 3. One-time retrospective correction review (already complete)
+
+The required addenda exist and were read this session:
+`20261102T183925Z-founder-charter-deployment-blocked.judicia-retro-addendum-20261122.md` and
+`20261102T193457Z-founder-constitution-correction.judicia-retro-addendum-20261122.md`. Both are
+dated, reference the exact prior report and disposition, identify the unsupported conclusions
+(host-side charter installation demanded; "byte-for-byte identical" claim treated as a current
+fact), record the Founder's withdrawal and the reverting commit `c7306335`, and preserve the
+originals. No new substantive evidence or independently identified error was found, so per the
+one-time instruction the review was **not repeated**. The withdrawn constitutional amendment has
+not been deployed and must not be.
+
+A bounded sample of other reviewed dispositions (Act 21 gate-recording cases, health/closure
+cases, transport-authority and SoringP1 conflation dispositions) was checked against the filed
+Git/board evidence in this cycle's frozen evidence. Where a prior disposition claimed
+"independently verified" but the underlying artifact was a reporter assertion or an inaccessible
+external repo, the filed records already carry an explicit limitation; I did not convert any
+such record into a verified success.
+
+## 4. Continuity obligations
+
+All `continuity_unverified` case files (`c1a00001`, `executive`, `innovation-centre`, `judiciary`)
+are already `verified_closed` or `auto_closed`, each with a matching `continuity/verified-*.json`
+carrying `verified_by: judiciary`, `verification_scope: external_effect_reconciled`, named
+previous/successor agents and a specific evidence reference. I found no open, unreconciled
+case requiring a new `verified-OFFICE.json`; none was written. A successful agent exit alone
+would not have sufficed.
+
+## 5. Founder priorities (Acts 8 and 9), measured
+
+**Quality (first).** Mixed. Real deliveries land with exact-commit gates (parity-v3 ballots and
+summons clears on `main`; external PRs with GitHub-hosted CI green), and CI was not improperly
+disabled. Against that: 90 open findings in the deterministic controller, 12 repeated-finding
+subjects, and a recurring class of **Act 21 exact-commit/tree gate-recording failures** on
+government/records changes (sampled PnP decision; many historical cases in the frozen evidence).
+A missing verification record is not proof tests were red; it is a genuine absence of positive
+evidence of the required gate, counted against a quality claim.
+
+**Timeliness (second).** Materially degraded by the integrator machinery. Two sustained stalls
+today (21:36→22:07Z per prior disposition; 22:31→23:03Z independently confirmed here). The
+queue serialises all deliveries behind one full-suite verification with an unbounded wait; the
+record-only ballots were delayed ~30+ minutes and only landed after self-recovery. The actor that
+fixed the symptom was queue resumption, not a bounded, fail-closed timeout.
+
+**Attention (third).** No `NEEDS-FOUNDER` request originated from the Judiciary this cycle;
+routine choices were made by accountable offices. The Founder was not asked to approve a
+technical timeout or a legal change. This is a positive observation, but it is a leading
+indicator only — low message volume is not by itself proof of conserved attention.
+
+No trade of substantial quality for superficial speed was found in the sampled cases; the
+dominant failure mode is the opposite — quality verification evidence missing while work sits
+on `main`.
+
+## 6. Sampling uncertainty, false positives and missing measurements
+
+- Four cases from a universe of 506 (0.8%) cannot estimate a population defect rate. Selection is
+  reproducible and could not be predicted from a public timestamp, but small-sample findings are
+  evidence of *existence*, not prevalence.
+- Host attribution on issues is inferred from board self-reports and author labels, not
+  independent host telemetry; CI on GitHub-hosted runners is expressly distinguished and was
+  never treated as agent execution.
+- External project repositories are not accessible from this host (unauthenticated GitHub reads
+  fail; no local clone for QAI/Proviral, Skrynia variants, etc.). Several "claimed delivery"
+  cases are therefore `inconclusive` rather than confirmed or refuted.
+- I did not re-run suites; green results are recorded digests/carriers. I did not observe the
+  earlier hung process tree live (it had exited), nor sample host load; the specific FIFO hang
+  point is reporter-supplied. The unbounded-wait mechanism is independently verified in code.
+- `unresolved_inconclusive` (120 signals) and `correction_not_effective` (11) dominate the
+  controller output; these are largely **lack of evidence**, not clean results and not proof of
+  misconduct. Treating either as a pass would be a false positive; treating them as guilt would
+  be a false negative.
+- State-dir audit outcomes are auditable assertions, not machine-verified proofs. Git-anchored
+  corrections remain the authoritative trail where Act 17 applies.
+
+## 7. Effectiveness of the Judiciary's own operations
+
+Observed this cycle: all four sampled verdicts were filed with case-specific evidence; the
+mandatory mailbox report received an independent disposition with named artifacts, claims tested,
+contrary evidence and limits, and was preserved rather than silently archived; the one-time
+retrospective corrections were verified complete and not repeated; continuity cases were checked
+and not re-filed. Twenty-five untracked predecessor judicial reports/addenda (2026-11-12 to
+2026-11-15) remain uncommitted in the judiciary worktree and are **not in `origin/main`** — they
+are not part of the Town's durable landed record. I preserved them untouched rather than
+rewriting or deleting another agent's work; this is a real durability/effectiveness limitation
+for Parliament to note.
+
+Self-assessment limits: the same model family produces both reporter and reviewer in many cases,
+so "independent" here means an independent *seat and evidence path*, not an independent
+substrate. My own measurement did not re-run tests or obtain host telemetry. A clean judicial
+process exit is not evidence of useful delivery.
+
+## 8. Measured effects of previously ratified corrections (evidence only)
+
+- **Auto-close after 20 clear observations (Founder directive 2026-11-16):** applied correctly.
+  The present mailbox case still has a firing signal (0 clear), so no auto-close occurred; I did
+  not manufacture a closure. 84 cases have auto-closed historically with machine records.
+- **Act 21 exact-commit/tree gate + Act 31 integration:** partially effective. Gates produce
